  "notes": "Drawn for the 777Fs (ten, the larger fleet), measured on B-18771 and B-18775 (right side, 2026) and checked on B-18781's left side (oblique): the passenger scheme's nose, belly and fin with cargo titles in place of the passenger title. Right-side 'at' values give the nose-most end of each word. The eight 747-400Fs differ in the titles: on B-18720 (left side, February 2026) 'CHINA / AIRLINES' is stacked in two lines of navy capitals behind the nose swath with periwinkle 'CARGO' after it, and no Chinese or aft title on that side; not drawn separately. No SkyTeam badge seen on the freighters.",
  "history": "Added with the cargo divisions (2026-11-13). The 777Fs (from 2020) were delivered in this scheme."
